  "revised": "2026-10-18",
  "source": "\"Modbus register DEEPSEA 86XXX\", 7-page register excerpt (GenComm pages 4 and 8), not a Deep Sea Electronics publication",
  "notes": [
    "Address = page * 256 + offset: page 4 (base 1024) holds the basic instrumentation and page 8 (base 2048) the named alarm conditions.",
    "32-bit values are sent high word first. Signed values are marked as such in the excerpt.",
    "Each named alarm register holds four 4-bit alarm conditions, the first alarm in bits 12-15.",
    "Unimplemented or out-of-range values read as the GenComm sentinel values (0xFFFF, 0x7FFF, ...).",
    "Serial settings follow the controller configuration; the 9600 8N2 values here are the GenComm defaults used by the other DSE maps."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "N",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 2,
  "byte_order": "big",
